WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.967 --> 00:00:02.601
-Hello, Kelly!
-Hello!

00:00:02.601 --> 00:00:03.970
-It is so --
-Oh, I'm trying to fix this.

00:00:03.970 --> 00:00:06.305
There we go. Is that good?
-Oh, that's so great.

00:00:06.305 --> 00:00:08.474
-I'm so close! [ Laughs ]

00:00:08.474 --> 00:00:09.709
-You're so close, but I --

00:00:09.709 --> 00:00:11.244
You're not close enough
for my money.

00:00:11.244 --> 00:00:13.179
I would of course much rather
see you in person,

00:00:13.179 --> 00:00:15.381
but we're doing what we can.
-I know.

00:00:15.381 --> 00:00:17.383
I'm, like, one of those people
that likes to hug,

00:00:17.383 --> 00:00:20.286
so this is definitely
not my cup of tea.

00:00:20.286 --> 00:00:22.255
-And I should say when I --

00:00:22.255 --> 00:00:24.790
I went out to L.A. and I was
a guest on your show once,

00:00:24.790 --> 00:00:28.694
and it is an incredibly warm
atmosphere, unsurprisingly,

00:00:28.694 --> 00:00:30.764
that you have built
in that show.

00:00:30.764 --> 00:00:34.700
I know you're coming back to
do a second season like this,

00:00:34.700 --> 00:00:36.102
with guests remotely.

00:00:36.102 --> 00:00:37.971
How are -- How are you guys
going about it?

00:00:37.971 --> 00:00:39.639
I mean, we have
a limited crew here.

00:00:39.639 --> 00:00:41.407
I'm assuming it'll be
the same for you.

00:00:41.407 --> 00:00:48.047
-Yeah. I mean, all
the restrictions you get,

00:00:48.047 --> 00:00:49.516
everybody's tested all the time
like crazy.

00:00:49.516 --> 00:00:50.783
Everybody's wearing
all the gear --

00:00:50.783 --> 00:00:53.185
and, even myself,

00:00:53.185 --> 00:00:56.188
unless I'm, like, on stage
and, like, working.

00:00:56.188 --> 00:00:58.157
And it's --
You know, we have virtual --

00:00:58.157 --> 00:01:00.894
You know, we have people
coming in virtually, like this,

00:01:00.894 --> 00:01:03.396
like, in an interview,
and then we also have --

00:01:03.396 --> 00:01:06.032
We're allowed like one,
tops two, I think,

00:01:06.032 --> 00:01:08.401
on the stage with us, and we all
have to be so far apart.

00:01:08.401 --> 00:01:10.469
Luckily, I have a big stage,
so that's possible.

00:01:10.469 --> 00:01:12.338
And then our audience
is, like, virtual.

00:01:12.338 --> 00:01:14.373
But it's kind of cool
in the sense --

00:01:14.373 --> 00:01:16.976
Because we've had people
from all over the world, now,

00:01:16.976 --> 00:01:19.145
at the show, and usually
it's, you know, whoever can --

00:01:19.145 --> 00:01:20.613
could've flown to L.A.
and whatever.

00:01:20.613 --> 00:01:22.782
But now we've had people
from all over the world, like,

00:01:22.782 --> 00:01:24.850
sitting in the audience, and
I'm getting to talk to them,

00:01:24.850 --> 00:01:26.785
and they're interacting
and everything.

00:01:26.785 --> 00:01:28.922
So that's actually pretty cool.

00:01:28.922 --> 00:01:31.858
But it's -- You know.
It's like your crew.

00:01:31.858 --> 00:01:34.560
We don't have everyone back yet.
And it's -- We're definitely --

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:36.696
Everyone's working
a little harder, obviously,

00:01:36.696 --> 00:01:38.364
to make it work.

00:01:38.364 --> 00:01:41.867
But I think it's good that all
our people have work, you know,

00:01:41.867 --> 00:01:45.405
and we're trying to get people
back as safely as possible

00:01:45.405 --> 00:01:47.673
just so -- I mean,
this is a big financial crisis

00:01:47.673 --> 00:01:48.908
for a lot of people.

00:01:48.908 --> 00:01:50.743
-It's both wonderful
to have a crew back.

00:01:50.743 --> 00:01:52.978
It's both wonderful to
have you back for an audience

00:01:52.978 --> 00:01:56.048
that has, in a very short time,
come to love your show.

00:01:56.048 --> 00:01:58.150
And I should congratulate you
since I last saw you.

00:01:58.150 --> 00:02:01.053
You guys won a Daytime Emmy.
Congratulations.

00:02:01.053 --> 00:02:02.955
-We did!

00:02:02.955 --> 00:02:05.358
We were so excited!
-I would imagine.

00:02:05.358 --> 00:02:08.260
-I didn't even
get to, like, see it.

00:02:08.260 --> 00:02:11.797
I feel gypped.
I totally missed it.

00:02:11.797 --> 00:02:13.832
And I was called,

00:02:13.832 --> 00:02:16.202
and it was hysterical, actually,
how I found out.

00:02:16.202 --> 00:02:17.770
Because I was just with my kids.

00:02:17.770 --> 00:02:20.639
I was honestly building Legos,
and it was a masterpiece.

00:02:20.639 --> 00:02:24.410
But I'm used to being
at the awards show, so you --

00:02:24.410 --> 00:02:26.579
You never watch them
because you're there.

00:02:26.579 --> 00:02:28.347
So, anyway, so that was --

00:02:28.347 --> 00:02:30.949
I feel gypped for
my first-time-ever Emmy.

00:02:30.949 --> 00:02:33.285
So, yeah, that was
really awesome because we --

00:02:33.285 --> 00:02:35.821
You know, we're still
finishing up our first season.

00:02:35.821 --> 00:02:38.524
And, man,
what a first season it was.

00:02:38.524 --> 00:02:41.527
What a way to start
a TV show. 2020.

00:02:41.527 --> 00:02:44.330
-Have they managed to get you
the Emmy in the mail yet?

00:02:44.330 --> 00:02:46.766
Has it shown up?
-No.

00:02:46.766 --> 00:02:48.000
I'm so excited, though.

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:50.269
I -- I'm literally --
I'm going to rub it in.

00:02:50.269 --> 00:02:52.538
I think just going to bring it
and set it on my "Voice" chair.

00:02:52.538 --> 00:02:54.373
-Yeah.
-Like, at "The Voice."

00:02:54.373 --> 00:02:55.808
And just be like,
"Oh, one of these?"

00:02:55.808 --> 00:02:58.211
Well, actually,
I guess John has one.

00:02:58.211 --> 00:03:00.345
He's got an EGOT.
He's, like, an EGOT winner.

00:03:00.345 --> 00:03:02.048
I just want to be an EGO.

00:03:02.048 --> 00:03:04.117
I just want an Oscar,
so I can have an EGO.

00:03:04.117 --> 00:03:05.351
I don't want an EGOT.
-That's true.

00:03:05.351 --> 00:03:06.686
I think most people with --

00:03:06.686 --> 00:03:09.322
Most people who only have
an Emmy also have an ego,

00:03:09.322 --> 00:03:10.857
so you're pretty close.

00:03:10.857 --> 00:03:12.792
But for those who don't know,
the EGOT is

00:03:12.792 --> 00:03:14.860
the Emmy, the Grammy,
the Oscar, and the Tony.

00:03:14.860 --> 00:03:16.395
You are now halfway there.

00:03:16.395 --> 00:03:19.599
You've, obviously, won
some Grammys over the years.

00:03:19.599 --> 00:03:22.502
What would you say
is most likely to happen next?

00:03:22.502 --> 00:03:25.771
Do you feel more confident
about the Oscar or the Tony?

00:03:25.771 --> 00:03:27.340
-I'm going to be honest.

00:03:27.340 --> 00:03:29.042
I don't feel confident
about either.

00:03:29.042 --> 00:03:31.277
[ Laughter ]

00:03:31.277 --> 00:03:36.282
I don't live in New York,
so the Tony will be hard.

00:03:36.282 --> 00:03:40.119
And, well, I'm not Meryl Streep.
I don't think that's shocking.

00:03:40.119 --> 00:03:42.922
So I don't see an Oscar
in the future.

00:03:42.922 --> 00:03:44.790
-See?
But there's a lot of paths.

00:03:44.790 --> 00:03:46.793
I think you're being
negative about this.

00:03:46.793 --> 00:03:51.297
First of all, you just let
somebody make a musical called,

00:03:51.297 --> 00:03:54.400
like, "Since U Been Gone,"
and it's just all your songs.

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:56.669
And you basically -- You're just
a producer on that, right?

00:03:56.669 --> 00:03:58.170
It still counts.

00:03:58.170 --> 00:03:59.772
-Well, then I feel like
you're cheating to get it.

00:03:59.772 --> 00:04:02.608
At this point, I'm satisfied
and content with EG.

00:04:02.608 --> 00:04:04.277
-Yeah, but, like,
it wasn't like John Legend

00:04:04.277 --> 00:04:06.812
won his Oscar
for being in a movie.

00:04:06.812 --> 00:04:09.282
You write a song for
a soundtrack. You can do that.

00:04:09.282 --> 00:04:11.350
-Okay. I can see
doing a song for it, okay.

00:04:11.350 --> 00:04:14.386
But, see, then I'd get the EGO.
-Yeah, there you go.

00:04:14.386 --> 00:04:16.689
All right, so we're saying
Oscar is more likely next.

00:04:16.689 --> 00:04:20.759
And we're saying you're, like,
98% confident within two years.

00:04:20.759 --> 00:04:23.029
-I'm...saying zero percent

00:04:23.029 --> 00:04:25.398
never going to get
the other two.

